    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Simbrŭvĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a district in Latium</i>, <i>abounding in hills and springs of water</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			371</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Simbrŭīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Simbruvium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 11, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stagna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 14, 22</span></i>
			.</div>
